{
  "name": "True Hide in Plain Sight",
  "type": "feat",
  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p>You may choose to take the Hide action and may stay hidden even when the conditions normally wouldn't allow you to, such as when you are in direct line of sight of a creature or you are standing in bright light. If you do so, you take a -5 penalty to your Dexterity (Stealth) check to hide. Depending on the circumstances, the DM may impose this penalty multiple times.</p><p>This feature does not allow you to bypass the conditions for hiding against creatures that perceive you with senses other than mundane sight or are able to perceive the true form of a shapechanger.</p>",
